# This repository is developed on Windows, where core.autocrlf=true converts
# LF to CRLF on checkout. Two kinds of file must not be converted, because they
# take part in byte-for-byte comparisons against freshly generated content:
#
#   src/**/*.js       the card builds its markup and CSS from template literals,
#                     so the line endings of the SOURCES end up inside the
#                     output the characterization baselines are compared with.
#                     A CRLF working copy would fail every baseline at once.
#   test/baseline/**  the characterization baselines are written and re-read by
#                     Node with LF newlines (see test/helpers/characterization.js).
#
# dist/ is deliberately absent from this list: the bundle is built locally and
# never stored here, so there is no checked-out copy for Git to convert.
#
# Everything else keeps the repository's normal handling.
src/**/*.js text eol=lf
test/baseline/** text eol=lf

# The characterization baselines are verbatim recordings of what the card
# actually emits, not hand-written files. The card's template literals do
# produce trailing whitespace inside the generated markup and CSS, so
# `git diff --check` would flag ~1500 lines in them on every change. Stripping
# that whitespace would corrupt the golden masters — the whole point is that
# they match the real output byte for byte. Exempting them keeps the whitespace
# check meaningful for the sources it is actually there to protect.
test/baseline/** -whitespace
